{# Fixed "GET QUOTE" bottom-of-viewport CTA bar.

   Pinned to the bottom of the viewport while the on-page quote form
   (#quote) is below the fold. The outer `.services-cta-bar-wrap` is
   position:fixed, 100vw, pointer-events:none; the inner
   container-fluid.col-md-10 > row > col-sm-12 structure mirrors the
   wrapper the site header uses in base.html.twig, so the bar's outer
   width matches the header's at every breakpoint. The anchor's click
   is intercepted by assets/js/services-cta.js for smooth scroll; an
   IntersectionObserver on #quote toggles .services-cta-bar--hidden
   to slide the bar off-screen once the quote form enters view.

   Included from:
     - templates/page/services.html.twig (anchor target is the on-page
       services-quote <section>)
     - templates/layouts/service-landing.html.twig (anchor target is
       the hero form column, gated on `landing_type != 'home'` so the
       homepage never renders the bar).

   The JS no-ops when `.services-cta-bar` isn't in the DOM, so
   including this partial is the only switch required to opt a page in. #}
<div class="services-cta-bar-wrap">
    <div class="container-fluid col-md-10">
        <div class="row">
            {# `.px-0` zeroes the default 15px column padding so the
               bar's rendered width exactly matches the site footer
               (`col-12 px-0 site-footer` in components/footer.html.twig).
               Negative row margins + zero column padding together
               extend both the bar and the footer to the full width
               of `.container-fluid.col-md-10` at every breakpoint. #}
            <div class="col-12 px-0">
                <a id="services-cta-bar" class="services-cta-bar" href="#quote" aria-label="Jump to Get Quote form">
                    <span class="services-cta-bar__label">Get Quote</span>
                    <span class="services-cta-bar__caret" aria-hidden="true">&#x25B2;</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
